# aef_sys.redefs - the six file system calls, renamed to the trampolines of
# src/aef_sys.c (the in-memory file and the system-call failure schedule).
#
# Applied by build.sh ONLY for a pin that sets DSL_SYSFAIL=1, and only to the
# DERIVED copy of the pin-built library archive under build/obj/<flav>/<t>/
# (the same copy the allocation rename writes, in the same llvm-objcopy call).
# Never to dsl.o, cli.o, libc.a, libc++, libunwind or the sanitizer runtime:
# cli.c reads the input with the real open/read/close before the program runs,
# so the driver's own input reading cannot fail, and musl's stdio reaches the
# kernel through its internal syscall wrappers, not these names, so the
# driver's stdout cannot either.
#
# Format: one `old new` pair per line; `#` starts a comment (the shape
# src/aef_alloc.redefs uses and llvm-objcopy --redefine-syms reads).
#
# DELIBERATELY ABSENT: open64, lseek64, fcntl64, pread, pwrite, readv, writev,
# creat, openat. zlib 1.4 at the pinned commit references none of them in any
# flavour (llvm-nm -u over libaef.a; under musl gzlib.c:12-16 picks lseek), so
# each pair here is conserved exactly, and build.sh's census refuses an archive
# that references any other name outside its allowlist
# (targets/<t>/sys.allow) -- a later pin that starts calling one of these
# fails the build instead of reaching the kernel unscheduled.
open aef_sys_open
read aef_sys_read
write aef_sys_write
lseek aef_sys_lseek
close aef_sys_close
fcntl aef_sys_fcntl
